What's the first car I came here with.
It has been serving me well, but

00:39:41.045 --> 00:39:44.715
the last year it was,
not really in use.

00:39:45.583 --> 00:39:48.119
So it’s going to be Ela’s car

00:39:48.119 --> 00:39:53.124
doing groceries, and being more independent

00:39:54.825 --> 00:39:57.461
She’s doing laundry.  Usually
we do this in town in a machine.

00:39:57.461 --> 00:40:00.464
But on a nice day like this,

00:40:00.765 --> 00:40:03.768
we can do it here.

00:44:32.202 --> 00:44:34.171
In a beautiful spot,

00:44:34.171 --> 00:44:38.342
Little cabin under a big  rock

00:44:39.576 --> 00:44:41.145
actually, Ela found it last year

00:44:41.145 --> 00:44:44.248
when she was camping up there
for her birthday.

00:44:46.016 --> 00:44:47.551
She spent the morning here.

00:44:47.551 --> 00:44:50.521
It's one of the many places
just around here

00:44:50.521 --> 00:44:53.190
where you can just hang out for an hour
or so.

00:44:53.190 --> 00:44:54.191
It's really peaceful.

00:44:55.159 --> 00:44:58.162
This beautiful chestnut tree

00:45:00.831 --> 00:45:01.065
Yeah.

00:45:01.065 --> 00:45:04.201
I'm finishing
the outer walls of the workshop.

00:45:04.868 --> 00:45:06.103
The inside I have to do.

00:45:06.103 --> 00:45:09.907
I think it's a day's work
or 2. Two days work.

00:45:10.774 --> 00:45:13.777
And then I'm going to start doing
the floor.

00:45:14.311 --> 00:45:16.447
I'm already configuring the workshop.

00:45:16.447 --> 00:45:19.149
How it's going to be laid out with,

00:45:19.149 --> 00:45:20.350
the tools.

00:45:20.350 --> 00:45:25.589
I think it's all going to be around
a central island, with a table saw,

00:45:26.223 --> 00:45:30.561
I'm going to get a new table saw
with a cast iron top and, a better motor.

00:45:30.561 --> 00:45:33.564
So because all the work
I'm going to do from now on has to be...

00:45:34.598 --> 00:45:38.102
a level up, basically. Most of the work was stone work

00:45:38.102 --> 00:45:41.071
and more rough carpentry work,

00:45:41.939 --> 00:45:44.842
you know, roof construction,

00:45:44.842 --> 00:45:47.978
but the next phase will be making doors
and windows.

00:45:48.112 --> 00:45:50.714
There’s going to be two doors
in second cabin,

00:45:50.714 --> 00:45:53.250
three actually, downstairs and two upstairs.

00:45:54.384 --> 00:45:55.352
Three windows there

00:45:55.352 --> 00:45:58.055
The front door of the first cabin I will redo

00:45:58.055 --> 00:46:01.058
because it's very weak door.

00:46:02.126 --> 00:46:03.861
Furniture, tables, probably.

00:46:03.861 --> 00:46:06.930
So there's a lot I'm going to make
for the cabins

00:46:07.331 --> 00:46:10.334
and the workshop.

00:46:10.434 --> 00:46:12.002
For that, I just need better tools.

00:46:12.002 --> 00:46:14.972
I've been waiting with investing in tools

00:46:15.072 --> 00:46:17.775
because everything rusts.

00:46:17.775 --> 00:46:19.576
All my tools that are in a second cabin.

00:46:19.576 --> 00:46:22.579
Because the roof is still open,
the doors and windows are open

00:46:23.413 --> 00:46:25.616
It's always very humid inside.

00:46:25.616 --> 00:46:29.987
And, it makes your tools rust,
especially after 4 years here.

00:46:30.721 --> 00:46:33.123
So first,

00:46:33.123 --> 00:46:36.126
I have to make the workshop
weather proof properly.

00:46:37.828 --> 00:46:40.864
That means I have to have a door
and the window, and then I can put

00:46:42.065 --> 00:46:45.302
something like a saw table with a cast
iron top,

00:46:45.302 --> 00:46:48.372
something which rusts very quickly in there.

00:46:50.874 --> 00:46:52.876
But sort of a central island with a table saw

00:46:52.876 --> 00:46:56.346
 together with a workbench with two vises,

00:46:57.214 --> 00:46:59.750
for hand woodworking,

00:46:59.750 --> 00:47:03.020
making joinery,
and then next to it, an outfeed table.

00:47:03.020 --> 00:47:07.124
So that's basically going to be
one big flat space where I can work on

00:47:08.158 --> 00:47:09.493
space to walk around.

00:47:09.493 --> 00:47:13.430
And then against the walls, cabinetry
on one side,

00:47:13.430 --> 00:47:16.433
a jointer planer to make wood flat,

00:47:17.701 --> 00:47:20.704
probably some dust collection as well.

00:47:20.971 --> 00:47:23.941
A wood stove is going to be in there.

00:47:25.442 --> 00:47:28.679
And all the cabinetry
is going to have like doors and drawers,

00:47:28.679 --> 00:47:32.783
but it's going to be on the same level,
like 90cm high or so.

00:47:34.751 --> 00:47:38.889
It makes it comfortable to work on everything at the same height.

00:47:39.423 --> 00:47:43.260
And then the miter saw
is probably staying outside at this point

00:47:44.461 --> 00:47:45.462
under the little roof.

00:47:45.462 --> 00:47:47.331
It's actually quite a good space
for the tools.

00:47:47.331 --> 00:47:50.968
It doesn't rust as much
there as inside the cabin

00:47:50.968 --> 00:47:53.971
because it's it's outside,
the sun shines there,

00:47:54.471 --> 00:48:00.844
and it's also protected from the humid air that comes in the night up from the valley.

00:48:01.578 --> 00:48:06.917
and a miter saw inside, it's going
to take up a lot of space, so

00:48:06.917 --> 00:48:09.987
 but yeah I'm going to slowly collect

00:48:11.922 --> 00:48:15.025
a bandsaw probably as well
I think I can use that.

00:48:15.392 --> 00:48:18.896
I saw some beautiful
old saws on Marketplace.

00:48:19.696 --> 00:48:24.801
So I'm going to be hunting
some old Italian tools

00:48:27.204 --> 00:48:29.973
Because they're a well built cast
iron heavy tools

00:48:29.973 --> 00:48:32.976
that just stay good forever.

00:48:33.844 --> 00:48:37.114
Probably need to polish up
some blades and bearings and

00:48:38.081 --> 00:48:40.884
clean it up and whatnot.

00:48:40.884 --> 00:48:42.586
So yeah,
that's going to be an exciting phase.

00:48:42.586 --> 00:48:45.589
Just slowly building up the workshop and,

00:48:46.490 --> 00:48:48.892
so that's going to be, well,
the week after next week.

00:48:48.892 --> 00:48:51.962
I think next week
I have some guys coming over to help

00:48:53.830 --> 00:48:54.932
with the spring clean up.

00:48:54.932 --> 00:48:56.900
Basically.

00:48:56.900 --> 00:49:01.071
Because this is the last week
before it's really starting to turn green

00:49:01.638 --> 00:49:04.641
and it's a good time to do some forestry
work,

00:49:05.108 --> 00:49:08.278
clean up the roads
and, to make some space.

00:49:08.712 --> 00:49:13.450
There's a lot of branches
and cut off things from cutting trees.

00:49:13.951 --> 00:49:16.486
And we need to clean up.

00:49:16.486 --> 00:49:19.289
So that's what we'll do next week.

